{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChPjjTXtNL4LZA2w9mHFR","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The network bounce to the triage engineer is built and tested, and it stays off. `servecmd` leaves the new `Deps.Network` unset, so a needs-network worker still ends `needs-human`, as in part 1.\n\nTests pass for closeout, triage, worker, roles, servecmd and reaper. I did not run `make lint`; I only ran `go vet` on the changed packages and `gofmt`. `gofmt` also flagged a testdata file under `internal/roles` that I did not touch.\n\n- **Bounce rules:** A first job with no branch or PR, and that did not push, is re-requested to `ard:triage:engineer`. Labels come off in this order: `ard:triage:engineer:done`, `ard:worker:<role>`, then `:running`. A not-found on removal counts as success. A resumed close-out after a failed removal posts one comment and finishes the removals.\n- **`needs-human` cases:** An existing branch or PR, a job that pushed, a second network round, or no triage engineer role all end `needs-human` with the list. The reason goes in the comment.\n- **`network-request.md`:** It is built from the record's `Plan.Network` only, marked untrusted, and listed as untrusted. It is added only when a bounced close-out exists.\n- **Prompts and docs:** The starter prompts under `internal/roles/` and `docs/proposal.md` are updated. The live `.ard/` prompts are untouched, so a human PR must follow.\n\nThe plan's test for \"`Deps.Network` unset as shipped\" is only a code comment in `servecmd/reaping.go`, because the closer's dependencies are private there. The existing needs-network tests still pass. The loop guard counts every closed worker needs-network record, including any from before the bounce existed.\n\nThe report is at `.ard/385/worker-engineer.md`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1038,"cache_read_input_tokens":79354,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1038},"output_tokens":600,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"fcf67195-41f3-4755-bbbb-55be9c472f0a","uuid":"4d69c37a-063c-4435-938b-6bd340cb8acd","timestamp":"2026-11-25T13:37:51.720Z","request_id":"req_011ChPjjTKk2xCJDSv9YTM5Y"}
